# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we show how to post-process noisy quantum samples to approximate the ground state of the nitrogen molecule $\\text{N}_2$ at equilibrium bond length, by using the [SQD Qiskit addon](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd) to implement the [sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) algorithm](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068). More details on the software can be found in the corresponding [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), including a [simple example](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/quickstart) to get started.\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, kami menunjukkan cara memproses sampel kuantum yang berhingar untuk menghampiri keadaan dasar molekul nitrogen $\\text{N}_2$ pada panjang ikatan keseimbangan, dengan menggunakan [SQD Qiskit addon](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd) untuk melaksanakan [algoritma pepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel (SQD)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068). Maklumat lanjut tentang perisian boleh didapati dalam [dokumentasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd) yang berkaitan, termasuk [contoh mudah](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/quickstart) untuk memulakan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nitrogen chemistry connects this example to sustainability through ammonia production for fertilizers. Understanding how catalysts activate nitrogen is part of research into less energy-intensive production methods. Calculating the ground state of an isolated nitrogen molecule introduces electronic-structure methods relevant to that broader challenge.\n"
msgstr "Kimia nitrogen menghubungkan contoh ini dengan kemampanan melalui pengeluaran ammonia untuk baja. Memahami cara pemangkin mengaktifkan nitrogen adalah sebahagian daripada penyelidikan ke arah kaedah pengeluaran yang kurang intensif tenaga. Mengira keadaan dasar bagi molekul nitrogen terasing memperkenalkan kaedah struktur elektronik yang relevan dengan cabaran yang lebih luas itu.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is recommended for users who are familiar with quantum chemistry: specifically, familiarity with finding ground state energies of a molecule. For a detailed walkthrough on the workflow,  refer to the [quantum diagonalization algorithm course](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms).\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini disyorkan untuk pengguna yang biasa dengan kimia kuantum: khususnya, kebiasaan dengan mencari tenaga keadaan dasar molekul. Untuk panduan terperinci tentang aliran kerja, rujuk [kursus algoritma pepenjuruan kuantum](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD is a technique for finding eigenvalues and eigenvectors of quantum operators, such as a quantum system Hamiltonian, by using quantum and distributed classical computing together. Classical distributed computing is used to process samples obtained from a quantum processor, and to project and diagonalize a target Hamiltonian in a subspace that they span. An SQD-based workflow has the following steps:\n"
msgstr "SQD ialah teknik untuk mencari nilai eigen dan vektor eigen bagi operator kuantum, seperti Hamiltonian sistem kuantum, dengan menggunakan pengkomputeran kuantum dan pengkomputeran klasik teragih bersama-sama. Pengkomputeran klasik teragih digunakan untuk memproses sampel yang diperoleh daripada pemproses kuantum, dan untuk mengunjur dan menyepelasi Hamiltonian sasaran dalam subruang yang dibentangnya. Aliran kerja berasaskan SQD mempunyai langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a circuit ansatz and apply it on a quantum computer to a reference state (in this case, the [Hartree-Fock](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartree%E2%80%93Fock_method) state).\n"
msgstr "Pilih ansatz Circuit dan gunakannya pada komputer kuantum kepada keadaan rujukan (dalam kes ini, keadaan [Hartree-Fock](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartree%E2%80%93Fock_method)).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample bitstrings from the resulting quantum state.\n"
msgstr "Ambil sampel rentetan bit daripada keadaan kuantum yang terhasil.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the *self-consistent configuration recovery* procedure on the bitstrings to obtain the ground state approximation.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan prosedur *pemulihan konfigurasi kendiri-konsisten* pada rentetan bit untuk mendapatkan penghampiran kepada keadaan dasar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD is known to work well when the target eigenstate is sparse: the wave function is supported in a set of basis states $\\mathcal{S} = \\{|x\\rangle \\}$ whose size does not increase exponentially with the size of the problem.\n"
msgstr "SQD diketahui berfungsi dengan baik apabila eigenstate sasaran adalah jarang: fungsi gelombang disokong dalam set keadaan asas $\\mathcal{S} = \\{|x\\rangle \\}$ yang saiznya tidak meningkat secara eksponen dengan saiz masalah.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum chemistry {#quantum-chemistry}"
msgstr "Kimia kuantum {#quantum-chemistry}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian of a molecular system can be written as\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian sistem molekul boleh ditulis sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+ \\frac12\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"h_{prqs} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+ \\frac12\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"h_{prqs} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the $h_{pr}$ and $h_{prqs}$ are complex numbers called molecular integrals that can be calculated from the specification of the molecule using a computer program. In this tutorial, we compute the integrals using the [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) software package.\n"
msgstr "di mana $h_{pr}$ dan $h_{prqs}$ ialah nombor kompleks yang dipanggil integral molekul yang boleh dikira daripada spesifikasi molekul menggunakan program komputer. Dalam tutorial ini, kami mengira integral menggunakan pakej perisian [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For details about how the molecular Hamiltonian is derived, consult a textbook on quantum chemistry (for example, *Modern Quantum Chemistry* by Szabo and Ostlund). For a high-level explanation of how quantum chemistry problems are mapped onto quantum computers, check out the lecture [*Mapping Problems to Qubits*](https://youtube.com/watch?v=TyFU6r8uEsE\\&t=900) from Qiskit Global Summer School 2024.\n"
msgstr "Untuk butiran tentang bagaimana Hamiltonian molekul diterbitkan, rujuk buku teks kimia kuantum (contohnya, *Modern Quantum Chemistry* oleh Szabo dan Ostlund). Untuk penjelasan peringkat tinggi tentang cara masalah kimia kuantum dipetakan ke komputer kuantum, semak kuliah [*Mapping Problems to qubits*](https://youtube.com/watch?v=TyFU6r8uEsE\\&t=900) dari Qiskit Global Summer School 2024.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) ansatz {#local-unitary-cluster-jastrow-lucj-ansatz}"
msgstr "Ansatz kluster unitari tempatan Jastrow (LUCJ) {#local-unitary-cluster-jastrow-lucj-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD requires a quantum circuit ansatz to draw samples from. In this tutorial, we'll use the [local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ)](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k) ansatz due to its combination of physical motivation and hardware-friendliness. We'll use [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) to construct the ansatz circuit.\n"
msgstr "SQD memerlukan ansatz Circuit kuantum untuk mengambil sampel. Dalam tutorial ini, kami akan menggunakan ansatz [kluster unitari tempatan Jastrow (LUCJ)](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k) kerana gabungan motivasi fizikal dan keramahan perkakasannya. Kami akan menggunakan [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) untuk membina Circuit ansatz.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-24 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The LUCJ ansatz adapts to QPUs with restricted qubit connectivity. The spin orbitals are mapped to qubits such that the ansatz does not require routing with SWAP gates. IBM&reg; hardware has either square lattice or heavy-hex lattice qubit topology. For the heavy-hex lattice, we can adopt a \"zig-zag\" pattern depicted below. In this pattern, orbitals with the same spin are mapped to qubits with a line topology (red and blue circles), and a connection between orbitals of different spin is present at every 4th spatial orbital, with the connection being facilitated by an ancilla qubit (purple circles).\n"
msgstr "Ansatz LUCJ menyesuaikan diri dengan QPU yang mempunyai kesambungan qubit terhad. Orbital spin dipetakan ke qubit supaya ansatz tidak memerlukan penghalaan dengan gate SWAP. Perkakasan IBM&reg; mempunyai topologi qubit kekisi segi empat atau kekisi segi enam berat. Untuk kekisi segi enam berat, kami boleh menggunakan corak \"zig-zag\" yang digambarkan di bawah. Dalam corak ini, orbital berspin sama dipetakan ke qubit dengan topologi garisan (bulatan merah dan biru), dan sambungan antara orbital berspin berbeza wujud pada setiap orbital ruang ke-4, dengan sambungan difasilitasi oleh qubit ancilla (bulatan ungu).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Qubit mapping diagram for the LUCJ ansatz on a heavy-hex lattice](/docs/images/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization/layout.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Qubit mapping diagram for the LUCJ ansatz on a heavy-hex lattice](/docs/images/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization/layout.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Self-consistent configuration recovery {#self-consistent-configuration-recovery}"
msgstr "Pemulihan konfigurasi kendiri-konsisten {#self-consistent-configuration-recovery}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The self-consistent configuration recovery procedure is designed to extract as much signal as possible from noisy quantum samples. Because the molecular Hamiltonian conserves particle number and spin Z, it makes sense to choose a circuit ansatz that also conserves these symmetries. When applied to the Hartree-Fock state, the resulting state has a fixed particle number and spin Z in the noiseless setting. Therefore, the spin-$\\alpha$ and spin-$\\beta$ halves of any bitstring sampled from this state should have the same [Hamming weight](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_weight) as in the Hartree-Fock state. Due to the presence of noise in current quantum processors, some measured bitstrings will violate this property. A simple form of postselection would discard these bitstrings, but this is wasteful because those bitstrings might still contain some signal. The self-consistent recovery procedure attempts to recover some of that signal in post-processing. The procedure is iterative and requires as input an estimate of the average occupancies of each orbital in the ground state, which is first computed from the raw samples. The procedure is run in a loop, and each iteration has the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Prosedur pemulihan konfigurasi kendiri-konsisten direka untuk mengekstrak sebanyak mungkin isyarat daripada sampel kuantum yang berhingar. Kerana Hamiltonian molekul memelihara nombor zarah dan spin Z, masuk akal untuk memilih ansatz Circuit yang juga memelihara simetri ini. Apabila digunakan pada keadaan Hartree-Fock, keadaan yang terhasil mempunyai nombor zarah dan spin Z yang tetap dalam tetapan tanpa hingar. Oleh itu, bahagian spin-$\\alpha$ dan spin-$\\beta$ bagi mana-mana rentetan bit yang disampling daripada keadaan ini harus mempunyai [berat Hamming](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_weight) yang sama seperti dalam keadaan Hartree-Fock. Disebabkan kehadiran hingar dalam pemproses kuantum semasa, sesetengah rentetan bit yang diukur akan melanggar sifat ini. Bentuk pemilihan pasca yang mudah adalah membuang rentetan bit ini, tetapi ini membazir kerana rentetan bit tersebut mungkin masih mengandungi beberapa isyarat. Prosedur pemulihan kendiri-konsisten cuba memulihkan sebahagian isyarat itu dalam pasca-pemprosesan. Prosedur ini adalah berulang dan memerlukan sebagai input anggaran purata penghunian setiap orbital dalam keadaan dasar, yang pertama kali dikira daripada sampel mentah. Prosedur dijalankan dalam gelung, dan setiap iterasi mempunyai langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each bitstring that violates the specified symmetries, flip its bits with a probabilistic procedure designed to bring the bitstring closer to the current estimate of the average orbital occupancies, to obtain a new bitstring.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap rentetan bit yang melanggar simetri yang ditetapkan, balikkan bitnya dengan prosedur kebarangkalian yang direka untuk membawa rentetan bit lebih dekat kepada anggaran semasa purata penghunian orbital, untuk mendapatkan rentetan bit baharu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect all of the old and new bitstrings that satisfy the symmetries, and divide a subsample of them into disjoint batches of a fixed size, chosen in advance.\n"
msgstr "Kumpulkan semua rentetan bit lama dan baharu yang memenuhi simetri, dan bahagikan subsampel daripadanya kepada kelompok tidak bertindih bersaiz tetap, yang dipilih terlebih dahulu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each batch of bitstrings, project the Hamiltonian into the subspace spanned by the corresponding basis vectors (see the [previous section](#quantum-chemistry) for a description of these basis vectors), and compute a ground state estimate of the projected Hamiltonian on a classical computer. Each bitstring consists of a spin-$\\alpha$ half and a spin-$\\beta$ half, each of which we call a *configuration interaction (CI) string*. The subspace of a batch is spanned by the basis vectors that pair every spin-$\\alpha$ CI string in the batch with every spin-$\\beta$ CI string in the batch.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap kelompok rentetan bit, unjurkan Hamiltonian ke dalam subruang yang dibentang oleh vektor asas yang sepadan (lihat [bahagian sebelumnya](#quantum-chemistry) untuk penerangan vektor asas ini), dan kira anggaran keadaan dasar bagi Hamiltonian yang diunjurkan pada komputer klasik. Setiap rentetan bit terdiri daripada separuh spin-$\\alpha$ dan separuh spin-$\\beta$, yang masing-masing kami panggil *rentetan configuration interaction (CI)*. Subruang bagi sesuatu kelompok dibentang oleh vektor asas yang memasangkan setiap rentetan CI spin-$\\alpha$ dalam kelompok dengan setiap rentetan CI spin-$\\beta$ dalam kelompok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trim each batch so that only the CI strings with the largest weight in the ground state estimate of that batch remain. Merge the remaining CI strings from all of the batches, and diagonalize the Hamiltonian again in the merged subspace.\n"
msgstr "Pangkas setiap kelompok supaya hanya rentetan CI dengan pemberat terbesar dalam anggaran keadaan dasar kelompok itu yang kekal. Gabungkan rentetan CI yang tinggal daripada semua kelompok, dan diagonalkan Hamiltonian sekali lagi dalam subruang yang digabungkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the estimate of the average orbital occupancies with the ground state estimate from the merged subspace. The highest-weight CI strings of the merged subspace are also carried over into the subspaces of the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Kemas kini anggaran purata penghunian orbital dengan anggaran keadaan dasar daripada subruang yang digabungkan. Rentetan CI berpemberat tertinggi bagi subruang yang digabungkan juga dibawa ke dalam subruang lelaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trim and merge operations in step 4 make up the [trim SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.01138) variant of the algorithm. Diagonalization of a single batch costs less than diagonalization of a subspace that holds every candidate CI string. Therefore, with trimming, SQD can select from a larger pool of sampled CI strings than it can diagonalize at one time.\n"
msgstr "Operasi pangkas dan gabung dalam langkah 4 membentuk varian [trim SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.01138) bagi algoritma ini. Pendiagonalan satu kelompok menelan kos yang lebih rendah daripada pendiagonalan subruang yang memuatkan setiap rentetan CI calon. Oleh itu, dengan pemangkasan, SQD boleh memilih daripada kumpulan rentetan CI bersampel yang lebih besar daripada yang mampu didiagonalkan sekali gus.\n"

